        # upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
        "//patches:0164-openroad-ram-read-drive-groups.patch",
        # 0165: generate_ram with more than one write port: each port's
        # take, its data's select in every bit's data mux, per eight bits
        # (a 128-bit word's take drove 128 data muxes). Not upstreamed;
        # retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
        "//patches:0165-openroad-ram-take-groups.patch",
        # 0166: generate_ram: a word of no more than eight bits, one group,
        # takes its write enable and each port's take without a group
        # buffer, which only added a level. Not upstreamed; retires at a
        # //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
        "//patches:0166-openroad-ram-one-group.patch",
        # 0167: generate_ram: a word of more than eight groups takes its
        # write enable and each port's take through a buffer per eight
        # groups (a 128-bit word's enable drove 16 group buffers). Not
        # upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
        "//patches:0167-openroad-ram-wide-word-tree.patch",
        # 0170: generate_ram: no pin within a pitch of a die corner (a via
        # from the first track along an edge lands outside the die,
        # DRT-0255), and the address pins the right edge cannot hold on
